        "like": 12
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you sideload the controllers along the pimax driver with the lighthouse driver (Four controllers will show up), use OpenVR-SpaceCalibrator to line them up, and disable the pimax controller copies with OpenVR-InputEmulator, you can actually use finger tracking. It seems like this is a bug where VRChat will only accept finger tracking from the lighthouse driver. Its as if it has been hardcoded specifically for that driver. Can we please get a fix? This is the same issue with SDraws Leap Motion Index emulator on github.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
